<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity up 0.01 pct wk to Feb 14.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity up 0.01 pct wk to Feb 14.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Thursday liquidity in the banking system grew 0.01 percent or two million sucres to 17.28 billion sucres in the week to February 14.</p>
<p>At the end of January, bank liquidity stood at 17.09 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the bank sector ended 1996 at 16.99 billion sucres, up 35.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
